issues:
TypeScript compilation fails in src/screens/RestoreScreen.tsx: The result of DocumentPicker.getDocumentAsync is typed as DocumentPickerResult which does not have 'type' or 'uri' properties, causing TS2339 errors on lines 20‑23. Cast the result to any or add proper type guards, e.g. `const result = await DocumentPicker.getDocumentAsync({ type: '*/*' }) as any; if (result.type === 'success' && result.uri) { … }`.

    Also import and use `Platform` from 'react-native' and update the imports to include `useRef` (replace `import React, { useState } from 'react';` with `import React, { useState, useRef } from 'react';`). Add `import { Platform } from 'react-native';`.

    Implement a web‑specific fallback for file selection: render a hidden `<input type="file" …>` (using a ref) and in `pickFile` call `fileInputRef.current?.click()` when `Platform.OS === 'web'`. Handle the `onChange` event to read the selected file as text and set `backupBlob`. This ensures a native file chooser is opened on web, satisfying the UI‑flow upload step.

    Example modifications (lines approximate):
    ```tsx
    // after other imports
    import { Platform } from 'react-native';
    const fileInputRef = useRef<any>(null);
    const pickFile = async () => {
      if (Platform.OS === 'web') {
        fileInputRef.current?.click();
        return;
      }
      try {
        const result = await DocumentPicker.getDocumentAsync({ type: '*/*' }) as any;
        if (result.type === 'success' && result.uri) {
          const content = await FileSystem.readAsStringAsync(result.uri, { encoding: FileSystem.EncodingType.UTF8 });
          setBackupBlob(content);
          setSnack('');
        }
      } catch {
        setSnack('Failed to pick file');
      }
    };
    ...
    <PrimaryButton label="Select backup file" variant="secondary" onPress={pickFile} disabled={loading} />
    {Platform.OS === 'web' && (
      <input
        type="file"
        accept="*/*"
        style={{ display: 'none' }}
        ref={fileInputRef}
        onChange={async (e) => {
          const file = e.target.files?.[0];
          if (file) {
            const text = await file.text();
            setBackupBlob(text);
            setSnack('');
          }
        }}
      />
    )}
    ```

- The UI primary flow validation fails at step 65 "upload button 'Select backup file'" because the button does not trigger a file chooser in the web environment. Adding the hidden file input and invoking its click (as described above) will cause the file chooser event, allowing the UI‑flow test to succeed.
